    "body": "Maintainer decision (question dialog, 2026-11-26) on the Outside region at the stock edge: \"Yes, to the edge\". For the material side Outside, the tool centre can go to the stock outline. Thus the cutter overhangs the stock by up to one tool radius, and each stock edge and corner is cut. A clamp at the stock edge needs a keep-out.\n\nThis confirms decision 2 of `docs/decisions/4025-kernel-region.md` on branch `issue/4025-kernel-region` (`cfef8048f`). The old 2D Offset planner keeps the tool centre one radius inside the stock outline; that difference is pinned and stays until the switch-over. The worker adds the maintainer's words to the decision file with the next push of this branch.",
